# SRG-APP-000915-WSR-000310  -  CAT II
# The web server must provide protected storage for cryptographic keys with
# organization-defined safeguards and/or hardware protected key store.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000915-WSR-000310
group:           V-264357
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-004910
control_rev5:    SC-28

contribution:    Splunk Web can name an organization-issued certificate and private key in
                 place of the auto-generated pair and can hold a password on that private
                 key, which is the key protection the web interface's configuration can
                 express.

governs:         web.conf - Configures the Splunk Web interface.

check:           web.conf [settings] privKeyPath not_equals $SPLUNK_HOME/etc/auth/splunkweb/privkey.pem
check:           web.conf [settings] serverCert not_equals $SPLUNK_HOME/etc/auth/splunkweb/cert.pem
check:           web.conf [settings] sslPassword non_empty
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          web.conf [settings] privKeyPath https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/web.conf
vendor:          web.conf [settings] serverCert https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/web.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Organization-defined safeguards for key storage, such as file system
                 permissions, disk encryption or a hardware protected key store, which the
                 check text leaves to the organization
external:        Any hardware security module or external key store, which web.conf does
                 not reference
external:        Operating system ownership and permission bits on the Splunk Web
                 certificate and key files
external:        The splunk.secret file and its permissions, which protect the stored
                 password's encryption

citation:        SRG-APP-000915-WSR-000310 check text; SPLK-CL-000330 fix text;
                 web.conf.spec:75-98
finding:         Splunk Web's private key is not protected to the extent the product
                 allows: privKeyPath and serverCert still name the auto-generated default
                 files, or sslPassword is unset so the private key is stored without a
                 password.
